tor. Inhibits cell proliferation by activating either CDKN1A/p21 transcription or RB1 transcription. [Isoform 1]: Binds CDKN1A promoter and activates its transcription; this activity is further potentiated in the presence of EP300 (synergistic) and ZBTB17/Miz-1 (additive). [Isoform 3]: Activates RB1 transcription most probably by antagonizing ZBTB17 repression of RB1. Does not bind directly RB1 promoter."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}